content:
The invoices table has 2 bad rows (created at t=538 and t=539, both after the v1.1 deploy at t=533), and the ledger has 1 of those 2 so far. The bad data clearly originates in invoice-agent. The VAT values are ~6.67× the amount rather than 0.15×, suggesting the new prompt is swapping amount and VAT roles (VAT ≈ amount × 6.67, which is the inverse of 0.15). No further investigation needed.

```json
{
  "investigate": [],
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "service": "invoice-agent",
      "kind": "bad_deploy",
      "mechanism": "The v1.1 deploy at t=533 introduced a new extraction prompt that inverts the VAT calculation (writing VAT ≈ amount / 0.15 instead of amount × 0.15), producing grossly inflated VAT and total values in the invoices table; sync-job then copies these bad values verbatim into the ledger.",
      "supporting": ["E1", "E3", "E8", "E9"],
      "refuting": [],
      "explains": ["I3_ledger_integrity"],
      "repair_plan": [
        {"action": "rollback_service", "params": {"service": "invoice-agent"}},
        {"action": "resync_ledger", "params": {}}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "invoice-agent v1.1's new extraction prompt inverts the VAT formula, writing VAT = amount / 0.15 instead of amount × 0.15 into the invoices table (2 bad rows at t=538–539), which sync-job propagates to the ledger; rollback of invoice-agent followed by resync_ledger will fix both tables."
}
```
